# Day 38

## Experiment Title

Integrating Docker with Maven Applications


## Objective

To understand how Docker can be integrated with Maven applications for containerized deployment.


## Theory

Docker and Maven can be integrated to simplify the deployment of Java applications inside containers. Maven is used to build and package the application, while Docker is used to create and manage application containers.

This integration helps developers automate the process of application building and deployment. Containerized deployment improves portability, consistency, and scalability of applications across different environments.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Docker Desktop

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Maven project directory.

Build the Java application using Maven.

Create a Docker configuration file for the application.

Generate a Docker image for the Maven application.

Run the Docker container and verify application execution.

Observe the container details using Docker Desktop.


## Output

The Maven application was packaged successfully.

A Docker image for the application was created successfully.

The application container executed successfully inside Docker.


## Result

Successfully integrated Docker with a Maven application for containerized deployment.
